<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qara Khitai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Qara Khitai, or Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a>, was a Central Asian state founded in the twelfth century by Khitan refugees from northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> after the fall of the Liao dynasty. It defeated the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-sanjar">Ahmad Sanjar</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qatwan">Battle of Qatwan</a> in 1141, destroying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> authority in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. Its lands later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and formed the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qara-khitai.jpg" alt="Qara Khitai" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_Liao.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Chagatai Khan (r. 1227–1242) received lands formerly belonging to the <b>Qara Khitai</b> and the Khwarazmian realm: Transoxiana (much of modern Uzbekistan), the Ili River valley, Kashgaria and the Tarim Basin, and the Semirechye steppe.</blockquote><a href="/empire/chagatai-empire">Chagatai Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1204, however, a Khwarazmian army supported by the <b>Qara Khitai</b> crushed him at Andkhud.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ghurid-sultanate">Ghurid Sultanate · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Western Kara-Khanids became vassals of the Seljuks after Malik-Shah I took Samarqand in 1089, and both branches later submitted to the <b>Qara Khitai</b> after the Battle of Qatwan in 1141.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kara-khanid-khanate">Kara-Khanid Khanate · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The empire reached its height under Ala ad-Din Muhammad II (r. 1200–1220), who overthrew the Ghurids in Afghanistan and the <b>Qara Khitai</b> in Transoxiana and ruled from western Iran to the Syr Darya.</blockquote><a href="/empire/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The prince Yelü Dashi had already led a band of followers west in 1124, and in Central Asia he founded the <b>Qara Khitai</b>, or Western Liao, which lasted until 1218.</blockquote><a href="/empire/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The fatal blow came from the <b>Qara Khitai</b>, a Sinicised Khitan steppe power, who defeated Sanjar at the Battle of Qatwan in 1141.</blockquote><a href="/empire/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
